OL,3,GNEWSAVeteran, 102, recalls German
OL,4,Atorpedo attack horror
OL,5,
OL,6,F"The Sergeant Major said to me, 'Do you
OL,7,Fsee that cruiser coming in? It's yours,
OL,8,Fyou join it in an hour's time'."
OL,10,FIt was a fateful conversation for
OL,11,F19-year-old John Eskdale. He went to
OL,12,Fsea aboard HMS Charybdis on 22 October
OL,13,F1943, but in the early hours of the
OL,14,Fnext day, in dark and freezing
OL,15,Fconditions, the cruiser was sunk by two
OL,16,FGerman torpedoes in the English
OL,17,FChannel.
OL,23,APub: 11-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
